course: dictionary
lesson: 14679
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word preserves can mean a food, a way of keeping things safe, or a special area. Context tells you which meaning is right. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about?
explain: «Grandma spent the afternoon making preserves in glass jars.» The jars and the cooking are the clues, so here preserves is a noun meaning jam or jelly kept in jars.
explain: «Salt preserves the fish, so it does not go bad.» Here preserves is a verb, and the sentence tells you what it does: it stops the fish going off. Try swapping in keeps from going bad, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The new nature preserve is a safe home for wolves.» This preserve is a noun meaning an area kept for one purpose. The clues are nature and a safe home for animals.
fact: Preserves has three main meanings: jam or jelly; to keep something safe or stop it going bad; and an area kept for one purpose.
fact: «Preserves» as a noun means jam, jelly or fruit cooked with sugar and kept in jars.
fact: «Preserves» as a verb means keeps something safe, unharmed or from going bad, as in «Ice preserves the mammoth for thousands of years.»
fact: «Preserve» as a noun can mean an area kept for one group or use, like a nature preserve.
fact: Salt, sugar, freezing and drying are all ways to preserve food.
exercise: «Grandma spent the afternoon making preserves in glass jars.» What are preserves here? | Children's games | A nature area for wildlife | *Jam or jelly kept in jars | Wooden boxes
exercise: «Salt preserves the fish, so it does not go bad.» What does preserves mean? | Makes something taste sweet | Sells fish at a market | Catches fish in a net | *Keeps something from going bad
exercise: «The new nature preserve is a safe home for wolves.» What does preserve mean here? | *An area kept safe for wildlife | A large shop | A race for runners | A type of wolf
test: «Ice preserves the mammoth for thousands of years.» What does preserves mean? | Digs up | *Keeps something safe and unharmed | Moves quickly | Eats
test: Which sentence uses preserves as a noun meaning food? | Ben preserves his old toys | The crowd preserves order | The farmer preserves the river | *Dad bought a jar of raspberry preserves
exam: «Football was the boys' preserve.» What does preserve mean in this sentence? | *An area or activity kept for one group | A shared treat | A game with a ball | A rule about fair play
